1
00:00:02,950 --> 00:00:06,016
Two mountain passes over ten thousand feet!

2
00:00:06,016 --> 00:00:09,296
One of the best lake views in all of Colorado!

3
00:00:09,296 --> 00:00:12,362
And a railroad town at the end of the line!

4
00:00:12,362 --> 00:00:13,360
Let's do this!

5
00:00:14,310 --> 00:00:23,552
This is Silverton to Durango: 48 miles of high passes and big views, and it picks up right where the Million Dollar Highway left off.

6
00:00:23,552 --> 00:00:26,610
Stay till the end for the full trip planner!

7
00:00:27,560 --> 00:00:28,650
Here's the plan!

8
00:00:28,650 --> 00:00:36,550
We leave Silverton, climb Molas Pass, hop over Coal Bank Pass, then cruise all the way down the valley into Durango!

9
00:00:37,500 --> 00:00:42,049
We're back in Silverton, and today we're heading south to Durango!

10
00:00:42,049 --> 00:00:46,530
Grab a coffee, because the views start the second you leave town.

11
00:00:47,480 --> 00:00:51,940
Right out of town, US 550 switchbacks straight up the mountainside.

12
00:00:51,940 --> 00:00:56,800
And keep an eye out on your left for Molas Lake, the perfect picnic spot!

13
00:00:57,750 --> 00:01:01,933
Welcome to Molas Pass, ten thousand nine hundred and ten feet!

14
00:01:01,933 --> 00:01:03,688
Seriously, pull over here.

15
00:01:03,688 --> 00:01:10,570
Those jagged peaks are the Grenadier Range, in the Weminuche, the biggest wilderness area in Colorado!

16
00:01:11,520 --> 00:01:15,989
Down from Molas, past Andrews Lake, and right back up again!

17
00:01:15,989 --> 00:01:20,310
Two passes over ten thousand feet, just seven miles apart!

18
00:01:21,260 --> 00:01:25,635
Coal Bank Pass, ten thousand six hundred and forty feet!

19
00:01:25,635 --> 00:01:28,525
And that big pointy peak right there?

20
00:01:28,525 --> 00:01:33,290
That's Engineer Mountain, almost thirteen thousand feet tall!

21
00:01:34,240 --> 00:01:38,717
Now it's a long, beautiful glide down into the Animas Valley!

22
00:01:38,717 --> 00:01:47,305
Fun stops on the way: Purgatory Resort, with a summer alpine coaster, and Trimble Hot Springs, just north of Durango.

23
00:01:47,305 --> 00:01:49,140
Your legs will thank you!

24
00:01:50,090 --> 00:01:51,398
Welcome to Durango!

25
00:01:51,398 --> 00:01:59,245
The railroad founded this town back in 1880, and you can still ride the steam train all the way back to Silverton.

26
00:01:59,245 --> 00:02:00,690
What a way to finish!

27
00:02:01,640 --> 00:02:03,637
And that's the drive!

28
00:02:03,637 --> 00:02:10,960
48 miles from Silverton to Durango, topping out at 10,910 feet on Molas Pass.

29
00:02:11,910 --> 00:02:15,070
Here's your trip planner, everything in one place.

30
00:02:15,070 --> 00:02:16,840
Pause and grab a screenshot!

31
00:02:20,410 --> 00:02:21,820
Thanks for riding along!

32
00:02:21,820 --> 00:02:27,460
Hit subscribe, and next time we're heading to Rocky Mountain National Park and Trail Ridge Road!
